---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
const irs='https://www.irs.gov/publications/p526';
const statute='https://uscode.house.gov/view.xhtml?req=granuleid:USC-prelim-title26-section170&num=0&edition=prelim';
const orp='https://www.oysterrecovery.org/get-involved/shell-recycling';
const md='https://services.marylandcomptroller.gov/taxes/en/tax-credits-deductions-and-subtractions?id=kb_article_view&sys_kb_id=733587b61b97d290168d6424604bcb8a&sysparm_rank=2&sysparm_tsqueryId=86ebb7b01bf136146cba8593604bcbe8';
const faq=[
 {q:'Can a restaurant claim a deduction for donated food?',a:'A federal enhanced deduction may apply to qualifying, apparently wholesome food inventory from any trade or business. Limits and documentation depend on entity type and facts. Ask your tax advisor.'},
 {q:'Can oyster shells be collected from my restaurant?',a:'The Oyster Recovery Partnership has a Shell Recycling Alliance with eligibility requirements, including geographic coverage, volume and storage. Check directly with the program for current pickup and fee terms.'}
];
const schema=[{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Service',name:'Restaurant waste and yield advisory',provider:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Tidewater Advisory LLC'}},{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:faq.map(x=>({'@type':'Question',name:x.q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:x.a}}))}];
---
<Base title="Restaurant Waste & Yield Advisory | Tidewater" description="Cut food waste, improve yield and build donation and recycling processes that fit restaurant operations." schema={schema}>
<section class="section"><div class="container alt-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Restaurant advisory</p><h1>Find the money going into the bin.</h1><p class="lead">Start with what you're buying, preparing, throwing away and donating. Build a practical system that cuts waste without making service harder.</p><a class="button" href="/contact">Ask about a waste audit</a></div></section>
<section class="section reverse"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">The first engagement</p><h2>Waste audit → yield fixes → operating routine.</h2><div class="grid-3"><div class="panel"><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Measure the loss</h3><p>Track trim, spoilage, overproduction and plate waste. Put quantities and costs against the categories that matter.</p></div><div class="panel"><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Fix the yield</h3><p>Review recipes, purchasing units, batch sizes, pars, prep methods and storage. Test changes with the team.</p></div><div class="panel"><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Recover what you can</h3><p>Establish safe donation and recycling workflows where qualified partners and local rules allow.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Food donation</p><h2>Don't throw away eligible food without checking the alternatives.</h2><p>Federal law offers an enhanced deduction for certain donated, apparently wholesome food inventory from businesses of different entity types. The general 15% cap applies to <strong>taxable income for C corporations</strong> and <strong>qualifying business net income for other entities</strong>, with additional rules and limits. <strong>Ask your tax advisor</strong> about eligibility, valuation and recordkeeping.</p><p class="fine">Sources: <a href={irs} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Publication 526</a> and <a href={statute} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">26 U.S.C. § 170(e)(3)(C)</a>. Tidewater does not provide tax advice.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section" style="background:var(--subtle)"><div class="container grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">Oyster shell recycling</p><h2>Keep the shell out of the dumpster.</h2><p>Oyster Recovery Partnership's <a href={orp} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Shell Recycling Alliance</a> serves qualifying restaurants in central Maryland, Washington, DC and Northern Virginia. It offers regular shell pickup for eligible operators. Confirm current pickup availability and any charges directly with the program.</p><p>Maryland <a href={md} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">previously offered an oyster-shell recycling tax credit of up to $1,500 a year</a>, but the state says no new credit could be earned for tax years beginning on or after January 1, 2023. Do not budget for that credit without verifying a change in law with your tax advisor.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Check program fit</h3><p>ORP lists conditions including location, 500 or more oysters served per week and appropriate covered shell storage. Source: <a href={orp} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Shell Recycling Alliance eligibility</a>.</p><p class="fine">[[TODO: Confirm any no-cost pickup commitment with ORP before advertising “free pickups.”]]</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Coming next</p><h2>Other ways to build the business.</h2><div class="grid-3"><div class="panel"><h3>Catering channels</h3><p>Identify and price repeatable off-premise catering opportunities.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Event space</h3><p>Put underused dining rooms and private areas to work.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Recruiting and retention</h3><p>Clarify roles, improve onboarding and reduce avoidable turnover.</p></div></div></div></section>
<CTA title="Know where your food cost is leaking." body="Start with a scoped conversation about waste, prep and recovery. No generic overhaul." href="/contact" label="Ask about a waste audit"/>
</Base>
